- (2) (Long-Range Projection) Solve the Poisson equation regarding Λ 𝑟 𝑠 : ∇ · ∇Λ 𝑟 𝑠 = ∇ · u 𝑀 𝑠→𝑟 on the grid to obtain Λ 𝑟 𝑠 . Then carry out a projection as u 𝑟 = u 𝑀 𝑠→𝑟 − ∇Λ 𝑟 𝑠 to ensure u 𝑟 satisfies ∇ · u 𝑟 = 0 .
In this scheme, particles are used to track flow maps and compute mapped velocity, while the grid or other discrete structures can be used to perform projection.

